From: Sergio Gómez <sergio.gdr@collabora.corp-partner.google.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jan 2025 18:03:15 -0500
Subject: ppd-cache.c: Fix IPP tag for pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported

pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported has the resolution syntax, but the
check added in 2.4.8 looks it up as a keyword, so it never matches and
is_pwg is always false. Printers whose only raster format is PWG Raster
(for example the Canon G3010 series, document-format-supported =
application/octet-stream,image/pwg-raster) are then rejected with "Printer
does not support required IPP attributes or document formats." by
"lpadmin -m everywhere" and by CUPS-Create-Local-Printer, which creates the
temporary queues used by print dialogs.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/OpenPrinting/cups/commit/63f5c71f0bd4ec1692162e153f033c120417c6af
Applied-Upstream: 2.4.12
Last-Update: 2026-10-25
---
 cups/ppd-cache.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/cups/ppd-cache.c
+++ b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -3545,7 +3545,7 @@
     is_apple = ippContainsString(attr, "image/urf") && (ippFindAttribute(supported, "urf-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL);
     is_pdf   = ippContainsString(attr, "application/pdf");
     is_pwg   = ippContainsString(attr, "image/pwg-raster") && !is_apple &&
-	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL) &&
+	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-resolution-supported", IPP_TAG_RESOLUTION) != NULL) &&
 	       (ippFindAttribute(supported, "pwg-raster-document-type-supported", IPP_TAG_KEYWORD) != NULL);

     if (ippContainsString(attr, "image/jpeg"))
